        {
            "_id": "8epgZjdKzgzj9eB5",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/TwoActions.webp",
            "name": "Princely Monologue",
            "sort": 800000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The frog prince is in his watery demesne</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The frog prince enraptures all those who play audience to his speech. Each creature in a @Template[type:emanation|distance:60] must attempt a @Check[will|dc:21] saving throw. The monologue lasts until the end of the frog prince's next turn, but he can Sustain it for up to 10 minutes. Each time he Sustains the monologue, any creature in the area who hasn't already attempted a saving throw against Princely Monologue must attempt the saving throw.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and becomes temporarily immune to Princely Monologue for 1 hour.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Fascinated] with the frog prince, but only for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is fascinated with the frog prince and can't willingly move away from the frog prince while it can hear the Princely Monologue.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, except the creature is also @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Stupefied]{Stupefied 2} while it can hear the frog prince's Princely Monologue.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
                "traits": {
                    "value": [
                        "auditory",
                        "concentrate",
                        "emotion",
                        "linguistic",
                        "mental"
                    ]
                }
            },
            "type": "action"
        },
        {
            "_id": "uAczaOxW2ybdDBQC",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/ThreeActions.webp",
            "name": "True Love's Bond",
            "sort": 900000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 3
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per year</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A humanoid creature who truly loves the frog prince kisses him</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The frog prince permanently transforms into a Small or Medium humanoid. He chooses his ancestry and the details of his appearance, and his equipment changes to suit his new form. The frog prince loses the fey trait and gains the humanoid trait. He has a land Speed of 25 feet and loses his swim Speed. He can use his rapier and water jet Strikes as normal. If the GM determines the humanoid creature's feelings aren't true love, this ability has no effect.</p>"
                },
                "frequency": {
                    "max": 1,
                    "per": "P1Y"
                },
                "publication": {
