            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>Lo and behold the tale of the frog prince, often depicted as a lost royal transformed by vile machinations. His daring, amphibious exploits are all in search of the destined love who'll elevate him to his true form and his rightful place upon the throne—or so it goes. When such stories persist in a region, whether as folk tales about a nearby pond or as placation for excitable children before bedtime, the innocent belief in their plight seemingly invokes an inexplicable, ancient power that gives form to frog princes. These fey appear as unusually large frogs, gifted with a capacity for expression atypical for most amphibians.</p>",
            "publication": {
